Every once in a while, someone discovers Lojban and comes on the list
to tell us how much they don't like it. But we can't do language
reform at so deep a level, even if we wanted to, so those
conversations are, to me, pointless and uninteresting.

This seems like another case of it. We lack the power to stop you
publishing your book, so what has me confused is, why don't you? What
are you trying to achieve here? Do you want or need something from us?
Does it just give you some kind of gratification to apply a lot of
negative adjectives to Lojban? Or what?

I've trawled through more of this endless discussion than I should
have. I am bored now. I don't want to read any more, so your reply is
probably the last email I will read on this topic. Make it concise.

-Matt

